{
  "_readme": [
    "RGS reference data for LEDGR (CMP-003, FR-ONB-005, FR-GL-005).",
    "",
    "This file is DATA, not a seed script. scripts/load_rgs_version.py loads it into",
    "rgs_version / rgs_element / rgs_profile / rgs_profile_element, and a future RGS",
    "release is another file loaded the same way - no migration, no deploy, no code",
    "change. See docs/decisions/ADR-026-chart-of-accounts.md.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE - READ THIS BEFORE A FILING SHIPS.",
    "source is 'provisional-subset'. The STRUCTURE here is real: RGS reference codes",
    "are hierarchical, prefixed B for balans and W for winst-en-verliesrekening, and",
    "the level-1 and level-2 codes below are the published ones. The deeper codes are",
    "in RGS's shape but have NOT been verified against the official publication, and",
    "the set is a starter chart rather than the ~4000-element MKB profile.",
    "",
    "Consequences, stated plainly: this dataset is enough to build and test the chart",
    "of accounts, the profile seeding and the version upgrade path against. It is NOT",
    "enough for CMP-002 (XAF 3.2 export carries RGS codes an inspector reads) or",
    "CMP-004 (SBR filings map through RGS). Loading it requires --allow-provisional,",
    "ledger.rgs_readiness() reports every administration pinned to it, and replacing",
    "it with the official publication from referentiegrootboekschema.nl is a GA",
    "blocker tracked in the ADR.",
    "",
    "Replacing it is a data change: load the official file as version 3.8, and every",
    "administration pinned to this one upgrades through the same path a real RGS",
    "release would use."
  ],

